---
const steps = ["Plan", "Change", "Check", "Continue"];
---
<div class="walkthrough" data-tabset>
  <div class="walkthrough-heading">
    <div><span class="mono-label">Contact list / Python</span><h3>Fix names with extra spaces.</h3></div>
    <p>An illustrated walkthrough of a recorded task.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="workflow-tabs tab-controls" data-tablist aria-label="Task walkthrough" hidden>
    {steps.map((step, index) => <button type="button" id={`step-tab-${index}`} data-tab aria-controls={`step-panel-${index}`}><span class="tab-number">0{index + 1}</span>{step}<span class="tab-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>)}
  </div>
  <section id="step-panel-0" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Plan</p><h4>Decide what<br />“fixed” means.</h4><p>The existing test caught padded names and entries made only of spaces. The agent recorded a focused plan before changing the code.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">A goal and its checks stay attached to the work.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record">
      <p class="record-label">Goal / Normalize contact names</p>
      <ul class="acceptance-list"><li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span> Trim surrounding whitespace.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span> Drop names that become empty.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span> Lowercase the remaining names.</li></ul>
      <div class="record-check"><span class="mono-label">Acceptance check</span><code>python3 -m unittest -q</code><span>Keep the existing test unchanged.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="step-panel-1" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Change</p><h4>Find the cause.<br />Change the source.</h4><p>The function filtered names before trimming them. A string containing spaces counted as a name.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">The agent used Magistr’s source tools to replace the function and record the edit.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record code-record">
      <p class="record-label">names.py / Recorded source change</p>
      <div class="code-change"><span class="change-label">Before</span><pre><code>def normalize_names(names):
    return [name.lower() for name in names if name]</code></pre></div>
      <div class="code-change added"><span class="change-label">After</span><pre><code>def normalize_names(names):
    stripped_names = (name.strip() for name in names)
    return [name.lower() for name in stripped_names if name]</code></pre></div>
      <p class="record-foot">One source file changed. The test stayed the same.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="step-panel-2" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Check</p><h4>Run the check.<br />Keep the evidence.</h4><p>The agent reproduced the failure, made the fix, then ran the same test through Magistr. The result was saved with the task.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">A recorded command and exit code make the result inspectable.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record verification-record">
      <p class="record-label">Recorded check / Contact list</p>
      <code class="check-command">python3 -m unittest -q</code>
      <div class="check-comparison"><div><span class="mono-label">Before the fix</span><strong class="failed-result">Failed</strong><span>1 test · exit 1</span></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="mono-label">After the fix</span><strong class="passed-result">Passed</strong><span>1 test · exit 0</span></div></div>
      <p class="record-foot">This result belongs to the recorded example. It is not a live test.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="step-panel-3" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Continue</p><h4>Start fresh.<br />Keep what matters.</h4><p>A new Codex session asked Magistr for the completed task. It recovered the defect, the source change and the passing test.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">The next session can review the work before deciding what comes next.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record resume-record">
      <p class="record-label">Saved work / Read in a fresh session</p>
      <dl><div><dt>Defect</dt><dd>Spaces survived; blank names stayed in the list.</dd></div><div><dt>Change</dt><dd>Trim once, drop empty names, then lowercase.</dd></div><div><dt>Check</dt><dd>One unchanged test passed. Exit code 0.</dd></div></dl>
      <a class="text-link" href="#evidence">Inspect the real sessions <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="walkthrough-foot"><span>Explanation based on the October 19 Contact list recordings.</span><a href="/docs/concepts#checking-your-work">How checks are recorded <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
</div>
<script>
  import "../scripts/tabs";
</script>
